- **Reasoning:** The existing code already includes `BORON_BLOCK` and `BERYLLIUM_BLOCK` as blocks, but lacks ores and raw forms. To add new boron and beryl ores, we need to create new blocks (`BORON_ORE`, `BERYLLIUM_ORE`) and their corresponding items. Raw forms (`RAW_BORON`, `RAW_BERYLLIUM`) should be added as items to match the existing `URANIUM_ORE_ITEM` pattern.

- **Solution:**  
  **ModBlocks.java**  
  ```java
  public static final DeferredBlock<Block> BORON_ORE = BLOCKS.registerBlock("boron_ore",
          properties -> new Block(BlockBehaviour.Properties.of()
                  .mapColor(MapColor.STONE)
                  .strength(2.5F, 3.0F)
                  .sound(SoundType.STONE)
                  .requiresCorrectToolForDrops()));

  public static final DeferredBlock<Block> BERYLLIUM_ORE = BLOCKS.registerBlock("beryllium_ore",
          properties -> new Block(BlockBehaviour.Properties.of()
                  .mapColor(MapColor.STONE)
                  .strength(2.5F, 3.0F)
                  .sound(SoundType.STONE)
                  .requiresCorrectToolForDrops()));
  ```

  **ModItems.java**  
  ```java
  public static final DeferredItem<Item> RAW_BORON = ITEMS.register("raw_boron",
          () -> new Item(new Item.Properties()));

  public static final DeferredItem<Item> RAW_BERYLLIUM = ITEMS.register("raw_beryllium",
          () -> new Item(new Item.Properties()));

  public static final DeferredItem<Item> BORON_ORE_ITEM = ITEMS.registerItem("boron_ore",
          properties -> new BlockItem(BORON_ORE.get(), properties));

  public static final DeferredItem<Item> BERYLLIUM_ORE_ITEM = ITEMS.registerItem("beryllium_ore",
          properties -> new BlockItem(BERYLLIUM_ORE.get(), properties));
  ```

- **Implementation:**  
  Use `CreateBlock` and `RegisterItem` methods to add the new blocks and items. Ensure the ore blocks have appropriate tool requirements and strength values. Raw forms are simple items to match existing patterns.

